From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 05:17:20 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 162/342] MediaPlayer: B_NV12 also for video without a color
 space of its own

10-bit HEVC has none that the Media Kit names, so the track supplier
settles on B_YCbCr422 and MediaPlayer never asked for B_NV12: the
decoder converted every frame, and couldn't hand frames to the overlay.
When the overlay takes B_NV12, it is tried first in that case too.

HEVC 1080p30 10-bit through the hardware decoder: MediaPlayer 3.7% ->
2.0% of the CPU.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/apps/mediaplayer/Controller.cpp | 9 +++++++--
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/apps/mediaplayer/Controller.cpp b/src/apps/mediaplayer/Controller.cpp
index efa89a5c1d..18c12e904f 100644
--- a/src/apps/mediaplayer/Controller.cpp
+++ b/src/apps/mediaplayer/Controller.cpp
@@ -366,8 +366,13 @@ Controller::SetTo(const PlaylistItemRef& item)
 	if (fVideoTrackSupplier != NULL) {
 		const media_format& format = fVideoTrackSupplier->Format();
 		preferredVideoFormat = format.u.raw_video.display.format;
-		if (useOverlays && preferredVideoFormat == B_RGB32
-			&& _OverlayNeedsYCbCr()) {
+		// B_YCbCr422 is what the supplier falls back to when the track has
+		// no color space of its own (10-bit HEVC, for one): B_NV12 may still
+		// be had, and shown without a copy.
+		if (useOverlays && ((preferredVideoFormat == B_RGB32
+				&& _OverlayNeedsYCbCr())
+			|| (preferredVideoFormat == B_YCbCr422
+				&& _OverlaySupports(B_NV12)))) {
 			// Switch the decoder now, to the overlay's row stride: doing it
 			// at the first frame takes long enough (more than a second for
 			// H.264) to lose the frames up to the next keyframe. NodeManager
